From 3b6c8ec45f535fb588e5a058db60810d420a8f81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:02:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] panvk: chunk large and indirect gpu_prerast draws on the
 GPU biblioklept

XFB, geometry shader and tessellation draws were limited to the 65536
invocations of one arena, and a single indirect draw could not be split
because its counts are unknown while recording. Indirect draws and the
draws that need more than one chunk (instance windows, strips with
primitive restart) now run two CS loops, compute and vertex/tiler, handing
the arena over with the tessellation ready/free syncs. A planner kernel
reads the draw, cuts strips at restart indices and repeats the strip
overlap, keeps the API base vertex and base instance through
chunk_vertex/chunk_instance, offsets the GS primitive ID and adds the
primitives generated of each chunk. The XFB offsets continue across
chunks through the existing counters. Chunks hold at most 2048 instances:
the lowering kernels hang the G615 with larger instance grids. The CPU
split now also handles triangle strips with adjacency.

Generated-by: LLM
